10. PHONE CALL ACCESS

Phone access is a required feature of RESOLVE.

During restricted sessions, the user must retain appropriate incoming and outgoing phone-call capability.

Incoming Calls

The device's existing phone system must remain capable of presenting incoming call UI.

The user should be able to:

- See an incoming call.
- Answer.
- Reject.
- End the call.

After the call finishes, the user should return to the Resolve Lock experience where the platform allows it.

Outgoing Calls

Display a small, elegant Phone action on the Lock Screen.

When tapped:

- Launch the existing system Dialer.
- Allow the user to enter or select a number.
- Allow the user to initiate the call.
- Keep the restricted-session countdown running.
- Return to RESOLVE when the call ends where supported.

Technical implementation

Prefer the existing Android system Dialer.

Do not unnecessarily replace the device's Default Dialer.

Do not implement a complete phone application or call-history system.

Use appropriate Telecom APIs to identify the default phone application.

Use only the packages genuinely necessary for system phone functionality in the Lock Task allowlist.

Do not hardcode assumed Huawei package names.

Do not grant broad Contacts, Call Log, or direct-call permissions without a demonstrated technical requirement.

Use the appropriate user-confirmed Dialer flow.

Timer behavior

Phone calls do not:

- Pause the Lock Duration.
- Reset the Lock Duration.
- Extend the session.
- Trigger recovery.
- Disable enforcement.

After a call ends, the same session continues with the correct remaining time.

Test incoming and outgoing calls on the target physical device.

Emergency calling must remain available.

